# These go to eleven (0.17.83): a knob that runs 0-100 and shows a plain 100 has one more notch, reading 11 in red. The setting stays 100;
# a notch down is 100 again. A knob with a unit or a name (or another range) stops at its top as before. (0.17.84) It shows at once, in the
# same turn (the screen redraws for it), and any number of knobs on a page can be at eleven together.
seed 0
wait 3000
tap ENV
wait 200
expect view 1
spin K1 120
wait 100
expect par0 100
spin K1 1
wait 40
expect par0 100
expect eleven 1
expect eleven0 1
shot eleven.png
spin K1 3
wait 100
expect eleven 1
expect par0 100
spin K1 -1
wait 100
expect eleven 0
expect par0 100
spin K1 -1
wait 100
expect par0 99
# two at once: Level and Bright both at eleven
spin K1 2
spin K2 120
spin K2 1
wait 100
expect eleven0 1
expect eleven9 1
expect eleven 2
expect par9 100
shot eleven_two.png
# a turn down from eleven: the first notch is 100, the rest go on from there; the other knob stays at eleven
spin K2 -5
wait 100
expect eleven9 0
expect par9 96
expect eleven0 1
